35,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Wow, I found some stuff! The island houses are about 5,400 yen per person per night, but food is extra. Also, all-in rates mean everyone pays the same, even if some people eat way more than others!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"That is an important detail, Sakura. I also found that renting a whole building results in a single, evenly divided bill, whereas separate rooms can lead to significant price differences between us, as we saw last time.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"That's interesting. I've been thinking about our group dynamic. It seems that when we stay in a shared house, it's harder to find a moment of quiet, whereas a town setting allows for more natural balance.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The transit data is concerning. The island option consumes two full days just for travel, and the spa valley has limited bus service. A city destination seems far more efficient, as the frequent trains eliminate the need for rigid planning.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found out that the island houses only have one bathroom for everyone, and the water might get cold. Also, the inns have very strict mealtimes and we'd all be in one room on futons.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"One bathroom for everyone?! That sounds like a giant puzzle to solve every morning! But wait, if we pay for the house as one big bill, does that mean we won't have to argue about who owes what?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,Exactly. A single bill for the whole building ensures a predictable cost for everyone from the start. It eliminates the risk of some of us paying significantly more than others due to room differences.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"That's true, Victoria. But thinking about Daisuke's point, one bathroom for five people might feel a bit crowded. I wonder if a town setting would give us more breathing room while still keeping us together?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"I agree with Midori. Beyond the bathroom issue, the island's travel time is a waste. Two days spent moving is unacceptable. A city destination is the only logical choice if we want to actually relax.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think the city might be better. The idea of everyone in one room on futons... and the strict mealtimes... it sounds a bit overwhelming. A room with a door would be much easier.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"A room with a door sounds boring! But if the city is faster to get to, we have more time for adventures! @Victoria, if we go to the city, can we still find a place with one big bill?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, that depends on the accommodation. While hotels usually bill per room, we could look for a city apartment or a rental house. That would give us the predictable total cost I prefer.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"That sounds like a wonderful compromise. A city apartment would give us that shared space for bonding, but the surrounding town would allow us to step away for a bit if we need a moment of peace.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Exactly. A city apartment minimizes transit time and avoids the rigid schedules of an inn. It is the most rational choice to ensure we return home rested rather than exhausted by the journey itself.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I agree. A city apartment sounds much better. I think I would feel more relaxed if we didn't have to follow a strict timetable for everything. It seems like the best choice for everyone.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"I'm totally on board with the city apartment! It's fast, we can have a big shared space, and it sounds like it solves everyone's worries. Let's do it! This is going to be the best trip ever!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. A city apartment provides the balance of efficiency and cost predictability we need. As long as we can secure a single rental bill, it is the most rational choice for the group.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,I'm very happy we've found a solution that considers everyone's needs. A city apartment will let us enjoy our time together while giving us the flexibility to breathe. I'm looking forward to it!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,It is settled then. The city option is the only one that respects our time and avoids unnecessary stress. I am satisfied with this decision. Let us proceed to the final vote.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm glad we all agree. I think I'll be able to sleep much better in a city apartment. I'm looking forward to going with everyone.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
